Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:35:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 26/59] PCI: rockchip: dw: stop the LTSSM trace work before
 suspend gates the clocks

rk_pcie_establish_link() arms trace_work, which re-arms itself every
5 s (also with the tracepoint off) and reads PCIE_CLIENT_DBG_FIFO_STATUS
when the tracepoint is on. It is cancelled on link failure and in
remove, not in rockchip_dw_pcie_suspend(), so a run between
rk_pcie_hardware_io_unconfig() and the next hardware_io_config() touches
a block with gated clocks. Short in a bcmdhd RESET, long in system
suspend.

Cancel the trace at no_l2, while clocks are still on. Link setup on
resume re-arms it. The !TRACING || !NO_GKI stub is empty. 6.12 t6.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01P6itje71iKPFBX7YKkfvRo
---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
index 54c03f1a6..a80098fc9 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-dw-rockchip.c
@@ -2286,6 +2286,8 @@ static int __maybe_unused rockchip_dw_pcie_suspend(struct device *dev)
 		dev_err(pci->dev, "Link isn't in L2 idle!\n");
 
 no_l2:
+	/* trace work reads APB; stop it before clocks go off */
+	rockchip_pcie_ltssm_trace(rk_pcie, false);
 	rk_pcie_disable_ltssm(rk_pcie);
 
 	ret = phy_validate(rk_pcie->phy, PHY_TYPE_PCIE, 0, NULL);
